{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistanceTheorems/ProjectiveRounding.lean | sed -n '1,140p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.DistanceTheorems.TensorSupport\n     2\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.Orthonormalization\n     3\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.Preliminaries.Completion\n     4\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.Preliminaries.Triangles.Core\n     5\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.StrategyRole.Algebra\n     6\t\n     7\t/-!\n     8\t# Projective rounding for consistent POVMs\n     9\t\n    10\tThis module proves the orthonormalization lemma `lem:ortho` with an explicit\n    11\terror constant: if a POVM `Q` on Alice's space and a POVM `R` on Bob's space are\n    12\t`δ`-consistent on a unit bipartite state `ψ`, then Alice has a projective\n    13\tmeasurement `P` on her original space with `P_a ⊗ 1` within `220 · δ^(1/4)` of\n    14\t`Q_a ⊗ 1` on `ψ`.\n    15\t\n    16\tThe argument passes to Alice's reduced state and follows the construction of the\n    17\tLDT orthonormalization theorem. Rounding the almost-projective effects of `Q` and\n    18\treducing their ranks gives a family of projectors `Q_a` whose ranges are almost\n    19\torthogonal; assembling those ranges into one auxiliary space gives an operator\n    20\t`X`, whose positive-Gram polar factor `X̂` is a coisometry; and pulling the block\n    21\tprojector of each outcome back along `X̂`, so that `P_a = X̂ᴴ T_a X̂`, gives a\n    22\tprojective family close to `Q`. The family `P` lives on Alice's original space\n    23\tand is completed to a measurement at one fixed outcome once its missing state\n    24\tmass has been shown to be small.\n    25\t\n    26\t## References\n    27\t\n    28\t- `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:131-153`\n    29\t- `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:390-423` (`lem:ortho`)\n    30\t- `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:425-464`\n    31\t  (`lem:ortho-explicit-constant`, the statement proved in this module)\n    32\t- `references/ldt-paper/orthonormalization.tex`\n    33\t-/\n    34\t\n    35\topen scoped BigOperators Matrix MatrixOrder ComplexOrder\n    36\t\n    37\tnamespace MIPStarRE.QPBT\n    38\t\n    39\topen MIPStarRE.LDT hiding Measurement\n    40\topen MIPStarRE.Quantum DistanceCalculus\n    41\topen MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective\n    42\t\n    43\tnoncomputable section\n    44\t\n    45\t/-- The normalized pure state whose vector is the given unit Euclidean vector. -/\n    46\tprivate noncomputable def roundPureState {ι : Type*}\n    47\t    [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]\n    48\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ ι) (hψ : ‖ψ‖ = 1) : PureState ι where\n    49\t  vector := ψ.ofLp\n    50\t  unit := by\n    51\t    calc\n    52\t      star ψ.ofLp ⬝ᵥ ψ.ofLp = ψ.ofLp ⬝ᵥ star ψ.ofLp := dotProduct_comm _ _\n    53\t      _ = inner ℂ ψ ψ := (EuclideanSpace.inner_eq_star_dotProduct ψ ψ).symm\n    54\t      _ = (‖ψ‖ ^ 2 : ℂ) := inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K ψ\n    55\t      _ = 1 := by rw [hψ]; norm_num\n    56\t\n    57\t/-- The QPBT vector quadratic form equals evaluation in `roundPureState`. -/\n    58\tprivate theorem round_stateQForm_eq_ev {ι : Type*}\n    59\t    [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]\n    60\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ ι) (hψ : ‖ψ‖ = 1) (T : Op ι) :\n    61\t    stateQForm ψ T = ev (roundPureState ψ hψ : QuantumState ι) T := by\n    62\t  rw [PureState.ev_eq_re_inner]\n    63\t  simp only [roundPureState]\n    64\t  change (inner ℂ ψ (WithLp.toLp 2 (T *ᵥ ψ.ofLp))).re =\n    65\t    (star ψ.ofLp ⬝ᵥ T *ᵥ ψ.ofLp).re\n    66\t  rw [EuclideanSpace.inner_eq_star_dotProduct, dotProduct_comm]\n    67\t\n    68\t/-- Evaluation of an operator square in `roundPureState` is the squared vector norm. -/\n    69\tprivate theorem round_ev_adjoint_mul_self_eq_norm_sq {ι : Type*}\n    70\t    [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]\n    71\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ ι) (hψ : ‖ψ‖ = 1) (T : Op ι) :\n    72\t    ev (roundPureState ψ hψ : QuantumState ι) (Tᴴ * T) =\n    73\t      ‖applyOperatorToState T ψ‖ ^ 2 := by\n    74\t  rw [← round_stateQForm_eq_ev]\n    75\t  symm\n    76\t  rw [@norm_sq_eq_re_inner ℂ]\n    77\t  unfold stateQForm applyOperatorToState\n    78\t  rw [Matrix.toEuclideanLin_conjTranspose_mul_self]\n    79\t  change (inner ℂ (Matrix.toEuclideanLin T ψ) (Matrix.toEuclideanLin T ψ)).re =\n    80\t    (inner ℂ ψ ((Matrix.toEuclideanLin T).adjoint (Matrix.toEuclideanLin T ψ))).re\n    81\t  rw [LinearMap.adjoint_inner_right]\n    82\t\n    83\t/-- Regard a nonempty finite coordinate set as an LDT finite Hilbert space. -/\n    84\tprivate def roundFiniteHilbertSpace (ι : Type*) [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n    85\t    [Nonempty ι] : FiniteHilbertSpace :=\n    86\t  { carrier := ι\n    87\t    instFintype := inferInstance\n    88\t    instDecidableEq := inferInstance\n    89\t    instNonempty := inferInstance }\n    90\t\n    91\t/-- A complete measurement on a nonzero finite space has a nonempty outcome type. -/\n    92\tprivate theorem round_measurement_outcome_nonempty {α ι : Type*}\n    93\t    [Fintype α] [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]\n    94\t    (M : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement α ι) : Nonempty α := by\n    95\t  classical\n    96\t  by_contra hα\n    97\t  haveI : IsEmpty α := not_nonempty_iff.mp hα\n    98\t  let i : ι := Classical.choice inferInstance\n    99\t  have heq := congrArg (fun X : Op ι => X i i) M.sum_eq_one\n   100\t  simp [Matrix.sum_apply] at heq\n   101\t\n   102\t/-- QPBT vector consistency is the LDT bipartite consistency relation on the\n   103\tassociated pure state and concrete measurements. -/\n   104\tprivate lemma round_consRel_of_consistencyDefect {ιA ιB α : Type*}\n   105\t    [Fintype ιA] [DecidableEq ιA] [Fintype ιB] [DecidableEq ιB]\n   106\t    [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α] [Nonempty ιA] [Nonempty ιB]\n   107\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (ιA × ιB)) (hψ : ‖ψ‖ = 1)\n   108\t    (Q : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement α ιA)\n   109\t    (R : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement α ιB) (δ : Error)\n   110\t    (hcons : consistencyDefect (uniformDistribution Unit)\n   111\t      (fun _ a => heteroKron (Q.effect a) 1)\n   112\t      (fun _ a => heteroKron 1 (R.effect a)) ψ ≤ δ) :\n   113\t    let ψp : PureState (ιA × ιB) := roundPureState ψ hψ\n   114\t    let HA : FiniteHilbertSpace := roundFiniteHilbertSpace ιA\n   115\t    let HB : FiniteHilbertSpace := roundFiniteHilbertSpace ιB\n   116\t    let A : MIPStarRE.LDT.Measurement α ιA :=\n   117\t      MatrixMeasurement.toMeasurement (H := HA) Q\n   118\t    let B : MIPStarRE.LDT.Measurement α ιB :=\n   119\t      MatrixMeasurement.toMeasurement (H := HB) R\n   120\t    ConsRel (ψp : QuantumState (ιA × ιB)) (uniformDistribution Unit)\n   121\t      (constSubMeasFamily A.toSubMeas) (constSubMeasFamily B.toSubMeas) δ := by\n   122\t    dsimp\n   123\t    constructor\n   124\t    rw [show bipartiteConsError\n   125\t        (roundPureState ψ hψ : QuantumState (ιA × ιB))\n   126\t        (uniformDistribution Unit)\n   127\t        (constSubMeasFamily\n   128\t          (MatrixSubmeasurement.toSubMeas (H := roundFiniteHilbertSpace ιA)\n   129\t            Q.toSubmeasurement))\n   130\t        (constSubMeasFamily\n   131\t          (MatrixSubmeasurement.toSubMeas (H := roundFiniteHilbertSpace ιB)\n   132\t            R.toSubmeasurement)) =\n   133\t        qBipartiteConsDefect\n   134\t          (roundPureState ψ hψ : QuantumState (ιA × ιB))\n   135\t          (MatrixSubmeasurement.toSubMeas (H := roundFiniteHilbertSpace ιA)\n   136\t            Q.toSubmeasurement)\n   137\t          (MatrixSubmeasurement.toSubMeas (H := roundFiniteHilbertSpace ιB)\n   138\t            R.toSubmeasurement) by\n   139\t      simp [bipartiteConsError, avgOver, uniformDistribution, constSubMeasFamily]]\n   140\t    rw [show qBipartiteConsDefect\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/StrategyClasses.lean | sed -n '1,210p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.Defs\n     2\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.Consistency\n     3\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.State\n     4\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.NaimarkFull\n     5\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.Preliminaries.Completion\n     6\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.StrategyBiProj.DirectSum\n     7\t\n     8\t/-! # Strategy classes and symmetric games\n     9\t\n    10\tThis module defines projective, commuting, consistent, PCC, and SPCC strategy\n    11\tpredicates from `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:89-183`, with source\n    12\tdefinitions in `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:68-180`.\n    13\t-/\n    14\t\n    15\tnamespace MIPStarRE.QPBT\n    16\t\n    17\tuniverse u\n    18\t\n    19\topen scoped BigOperators Matrix MatrixOrder ComplexOrder\n    20\t\n    21\topen MIPStarRE.LDT MIPStarRE.Quantum\n    22\t\n    23\t/-- Projectivity from `def:projective-strategy-general`, blueprint\n    24\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:90-101`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:68-72`. -/\n    25\tdef Strategy.IsProjective {G : Game} (S : Strategy G) : Prop :=\n    26\t  (∀ x, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsProjective (S.A x)) ∧\n    27\t    ∀ y, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsProjective (S.B y)\n    28\t\n    29\t/-- Symmetric games from `def:symmetric-game`, blueprint\n    30\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:100-109`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:74-92`.\n    31\tThe question and answer alphabets are each represented by a single shared type,\n    32\tmatching the source notation. -/\n    33\tstructure SymmetricGame where\n    34\t  Question : Type\n    35\t  Answer : Type\n    36\t  [questionFintype : Fintype Question]\n    37\t  [answerFintype : Fintype Answer]\n    38\t  [questionDecidableEq : DecidableEq Question]\n    39\t  [answerDecidableEq : DecidableEq Answer]\n    40\t  μ : Distribution (Question × Question)\n    41\t  μ_prob : μ.IsProbability\n    42\t  μ_symm : ∀ x y, μ.weight (x, y) = μ.weight (y, x)\n    43\t  decide : Question → Question → Answer → Answer → Bool\n    44\t  decide_symm : ∀ x y a b, decide x y a b = decide y x b a\n    45\t\n    46\tattribute [instance] SymmetricGame.questionFintype SymmetricGame.answerFintype\n    47\t  SymmetricGame.questionDecidableEq SymmetricGame.answerDecidableEq\n    48\t\n    49\t/-- Regard a symmetric game as a game with equal question and answer types;\n    50\t`def:symmetric-game`, blueprint\n    51\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:100-109`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:74-92`. -/\n    52\tdef SymmetricGame.toGame (G : SymmetricGame) : Game where\n    53\t  QuestionA := G.Question\n    54\t  QuestionB := G.Question\n    55\t  AnswerA := G.Answer\n    56\t  AnswerB := G.Answer\n    57\t  μ := G.μ\n    58\t  μ_prob := G.μ_prob\n    59\t  decide := G.decide\n    60\t\n    61\t/-- Symmetric strategies from `def:symmetric-game`, blueprint\n    62\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:100-109`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:74-92`.\n    63\tThe two local spaces and measurement families are identified, as in the source\n    64\tdefinition. -/\n    65\tstructure SymmetricStrategy (G : SymmetricGame) where\n    66\t  ι : Type\n    67\t  [ιFintype : Fintype ι]\n    68\t  [ιDecidableEq : DecidableEq ι]\n    69\t  ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (ι × ι)\n    70\t  ψ_norm : ‖ψ‖ = 1\n    71\t  ψ_swap : reindexState (Equiv.prodComm ι ι) ψ = ψ\n    72\t  M : G.Question → MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement G.Answer ι\n    73\t\n    74\tattribute [instance] SymmetricStrategy.ιFintype SymmetricStrategy.ιDecidableEq\n    75\t\n    76\t/-- Regard a symmetric strategy as a strategy using the same local space and\n    77\tmeasurement family for both players; `def:symmetric-game`, blueprint\n    78\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:100-109`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:74-92`. -/\n    79\tdef SymmetricStrategy.toStrategy {G : SymmetricGame} (S : SymmetricStrategy G) :\n    80\t    Strategy G.toGame where\n    81\t  ιA := S.ι\n    82\t  ιB := S.ι\n    83\t  ψ := S.ψ\n    84\t  ψ_norm := S.ψ_norm\n    85\t  A := S.M\n    86\t  B := S.M\n    87\t\n    88\t/-- Common-space commutation from `def:comm-strategy`, blueprint\n    89\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:141-150`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:132-142`. -/\n    90\tdef IsCommutingOn {X Y α β ι : Type*}\n    91\t    [Fintype X] [DecidableEq X] [Fintype Y] [DecidableEq Y]\n    92\t    [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α] [Fintype β]\n    93\t    [DecidableEq β] [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n    94\t    (μ : Distribution (X × Y))\n    95\t    (A : X → MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement α ι)\n    96\t    (B : Y → MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement β ι) : Prop :=\n    97\t  ∀ x y, 0 < μ.weight (x, y) → ∀ a b, Commute ((A x).effect a) ((B y).effect b)\n    98\t\n    99\tprivate def transportOp {d₁ d₂ : Type u} (h : d₁ = d₂) (M : Op d₂) : Op d₁ :=\n   100\t  h.symm ▸ M\n   101\t\n   102\t/-- Transported common-space form of `def:comm-strategy`, blueprint\n   103\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:141-150`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:132-142`. -/\n   104\tdef Strategy.IsCommuting {G : Game} (S : Strategy G) (hι : S.ιA = S.ιB) : Prop :=\n   105\t  ∀ x y, 0 < G.μ.weight (x, y) → ∀ a b,\n   106\t    Commute ((S.A x).effect a) (transportOp hι ((S.B y).effect b))\n   107\t\n   108\t/-- Measurement consistency from `def:consistent-measurement`, blueprint\n   109\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:152-161`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:144-160`. -/\n   110\tdef Measurement.IsConsistentOn {α ι : Type*}\n   111\t    [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α] [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n   112\t    (M : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement α ι)\n   113\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (ι × ι)) : Prop :=\n   114\t  ∀ a, (heteroKron (M.effect a) 1).mulVec ψ =\n   115\t    (heteroKron 1 (M.effect a)).mulVec ψ\n   116\t\n   117\t/-- General strategy consistency from `def:consistent-strategy`, blueprint\n   118\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:169-174`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:162-174`. -/\n   119\tdef IsConsistentStrategyOn {X Y α β ι : Type*}\n   120\t    [Fintype X] [DecidableEq X] [Fintype Y] [DecidableEq Y]\n   121\t    [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α] [Fintype β] [DecidableEq β]\n   122\t    [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n   123\t    (A : X → MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement α ι)\n   124\t    (B : Y → MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement β ι)\n   125\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (ι × ι)) : Prop :=\n   126\t  (∀ x, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsConsistentOn (A x) ψ) ∧\n   127\t    ∀ y, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsConsistentOn (B y) ψ\n   128\t\n   129\t/-- Symmetric strategy consistency from `def:consistent-strategy`, blueprint\n   130\t`ch12_qpbt_games.tex:169-174`, paper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:162-174`. -/\n   131\tdef SymmetricStrategy.IsConsistent {G : SymmetricGame}\n   132\t    (S : SymmetricStrategy G) : Prop :=\n   133\t  ∀ x, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsConsistentOn (S.M x) S.ψ\n   134\t\n   135\t/-- The PCC predicate `def:spcc`, blueprint `ch12_qpbt_games.tex:178-183`,\n   136\tpaper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:176-180`. -/\n   137\tdef Strategy.IsPCC {G : Game} {ι : Type*}\n   138\t    [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n   139\t    (μ : Distribution (G.QuestionA × G.QuestionB))\n   140\t    (A : G.QuestionA → MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement G.AnswerA ι)\n   141\t    (B : G.QuestionB → MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement G.AnswerB ι)\n   142\t  (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (ι × ι)) : Prop :=\n   143\t  (∀ x, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsProjective (A x)) ∧\n   144\t    (∀ y, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsProjective (B y)) ∧\n   145\t    IsConsistentStrategyOn A B ψ ∧ IsCommutingOn μ A B\n   146\t\n   147\t/-- The SPCC predicate `def:spcc`, blueprint `ch12_qpbt_games.tex:178-183`,\n   148\tpaper `06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:176-180`. -/\n   149\tdef SymmetricStrategy.IsSPCC {G : SymmetricGame}\n   150\t  (S : SymmetricStrategy G) : Prop :=\n   151\t  (∀ x, MIPStarRE.QPBT.Measurement.IsProjective (S.M x)) ∧ S.IsConsistent ∧\n   152\t    IsCommutingOn G.μ S.M S.M\n   153\t\n   154\tnoncomputable section\n   155\t\n   156\topen MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective\n   157\topen MIPStarRE.LDT.Preliminaries\n   158\t\n   159\t/-- The real quadratic form of an operator evaluated on a finite vector. -/\n   160\tprivate def vectorQForm {I : Type*} [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I]\n   161\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ I) (A : Op I) : ℝ :=\n   162\t  (inner ℂ ψ (Matrix.toEuclideanLin A ψ)).re\n   163\t\n   164\t/-- Embed a bipartite state into the distinguished Naimark ancilla coordinates. -/\n   165\tprivate def padState\n   166\t    {I J α β : Type*} [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I]\n   167\t    [Fintype J] [DecidableEq J] [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α]\n   168\t    [Fintype β] [DecidableEq β]\n   169\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (I × J)) :\n   170\t    EuclideanSpace ℂ ((I × Option α) × (J × Option β)) :=\n   171\t  (EuclideanSpace.equiv ((I × Option α) × (J × Option β)) ℂ).symm\n   172\t    (fun p => if p.1.2 = none ∧ p.2.2 = none then ψ.ofLp (p.1.1, p.2.1) else 0)\n   173\t\n   174\t/-- Padding a state by zero ancilla coordinates preserves its norm. -/\n   175\tprivate theorem padState_norm\n   176\t    {I J α β : Type*} [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I]\n   177\t    [Fintype J] [DecidableEq J] [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α]\n   178\t    [Fintype β] [DecidableEq β]\n   179\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (I × J)) :\n   180\t    ‖padState (α := α) (β := β) ψ‖ = ‖ψ‖ := by\n   181\t  apply (sq_eq_sq₀ (norm_nonneg _) (norm_nonneg _)).mp\n   182\t  rw [EuclideanSpace.norm_sq_eq, EuclideanSpace.norm_sq_eq]\n   183\t  simp [padState, Fintype.sum_prod_type]\n   184\t\n   185\t/-- The padded-state quadratic form depends only on the distinguished\n   186\tcompression of each local operator. -/\n   187\tprivate theorem stateQForm_padState\n   188\t    {I J α β : Type*} [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I]\n   189\t    [Fintype J] [DecidableEq J] [Fintype α] [DecidableEq α]\n   190\t    [Fintype β] [DecidableEq β]\n   191\t    (ψ : EuclideanSpace ℂ (I × J))\n   192\t    (A : Op I) (B : Op J)\n   193\t    (A' : Op (I × Option α)) (B' : Op (J × Option β))\n   194\t    (hA : ∀ i j, A' (i, none) (j, none) = A i j)\n   195\t    (hB : ∀ i j, B' (i, none) (j, none) = B i j) :\n   196\t    vectorQForm (padState (α := α) (β := β) ψ) (heteroKron A' B') =\n   197\t      vectorQForm ψ (heteroKron A B) := by\n   198\t  unfold vectorQForm\n   199\t  rw [EuclideanSpace.inner_eq_star_dotProduct, EuclideanSpace.inner_eq_star_dotProduct]\n   200\t  change Complex.re (∑ p : (I × Option α) × (J × Option β),\n   201\t      (∑ q : (I × Option α) × (J × Option β),\n   202\t        heteroKron A' B' p q *\n   203\t          (padState (α := α) (β := β) ψ).ofLp q) *\n   204\t        star (padState (α := α) (β := β) ψ).ofLp p) =\n   205\t    Complex.re (∑ p : I × J,\n   206\t      (∑ q : I × J, heteroKron A B p q * ψ.ofLp q) * star ψ.ofLp p)\n   207\t  simp [padState, heteroKron, Matrix.kronecker, Fintype.sum_prod_type, hA, hB]\n   208\t\n   209\t/-- Choose the one-measurement Naimark dilation data for a POVM. -/\n   210\tprivate def oneMeasData\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
