{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex | sed -n '215,440p'\"","aggregated_output":"   215\t\t\\[\n   216\t\t\tA^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\simeq_\\delta \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a\n   217\t\t\\]\n   218\t\ton state $\\ket{\\psi}$ and distribution $\\mu$ if\n   219\t\t\\[\n   220\t\t\t\\E_{x \\sim \\mu} \\sum_{a \\ne b} \\bra{\\psi} A^x_a \\ot B^x_b \\ket{\\psi} = O(\\delta)\\,.\n   221\t\t\\]\n   222\t\tIn this case we say that $\\{A^x_a\\}$ and $\\{B^x_a\\}$ are \\emph{$\\delta$-consistent} on $\\ket{\\psi}$. As in Definition~\\ref{def:state-distance}, the $O(\\cdot)$ refers to families of POVMs and states indexed by an implicit parameter $n \\in \\N$, and is taken as $n \\to \\infty$.\n   223\t\\end{definition}\n   224\t\n   225\tA measurement that is consistent on $\\ket{\\psi}$ in the sense of Definition~\\ref{def:consistent-measurement} is $0$-consistent with itself on the same state under the singleton distribution, and vice versa: if $\\sum_a \\bra{\\psi} M_a \\ot M_a \\ket{\\psi} = 1$, then $M_a \\ot \\Id\\, \\ket{\\psi} = \\Id \\ot M_a\\, \\ket{\\psi}$ for every $a$, by the equality case of the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality applied outcome by outcome.\n   226\t\n   227\t% The source (references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:257-274) states this\n   228\t% definition for pairs of POVMs but applies the relation to arbitrary operator families:\n   229\t% to plain operators at 06:313-330, to sets of matrices at 06:364-380, and to products and\n   230\t% commutators, compared against the zero family, at 06:409-445. The general form below,\n   231\t% for arbitrary finite families of operators, is the one of the NEEXP source\n   232\t% (references/neexp-paper/05_quantum_preliminaries.tex:385-391), from which the distance\n   233\t% calculus is imported; the POVM case is singled out after the display.\n   234\t\\begin{definition}[State-dependent distance between operator families]\\label{def:povm-distance}\n   235\t\t\\uses{def:povm-conventions, def:state-distance}\n   236\t\tLet $\\mathcal X$ and $\\mathcal A$ be finite sets and $\\mu$ a distribution on $\\mathcal X$. Let $\\ket{\\psi} \\in \\mathcal H$ be a quantum state, and for all $x \\in \\mathcal X$ let $\\{M^x_a\\}_{a \\in \\mathcal A}$ and $\\{N^x_a\\}_{a \\in \\mathcal A}$ be two families of linear operators on $\\mathcal H$. We say that \\emph{$\\{M^x_a\\}$ and $\\{N^x_a\\}$ are $\\delta$-close on state $\\ket{\\psi}$ and under distribution $\\mu$} if\n   237\t\t\\[\n   238\t\t\t\\E_{x \\sim \\mu} \\sum_a \\lVert (M^x_a - N^x_a)\\, \\ket{\\psi} \\rVert^2 \\le O(\\delta)\\,,\n   239\t\t\\]\n   240\t\tand we write $M^x_a \\approx_\\delta N^x_a$ to denote this when the state $\\ket{\\psi}$ and the distribution $\\mu$ are clear from context. This distance is referred to as the \\emph{state-dependent} distance. The principal case is that in which $\\{M^x_a\\}$ and $\\{N^x_a\\}$ are POVMs on $\\mathcal H$, and we then speak of the state-dependent distance between the POVMs; but the relation is used for arbitrary operator families --- for instance for products of measurement operators, or for commutators compared against the identically zero family, as in Lemma~\\ref{lem:commutation-analysis} below.\n   241\t\\end{definition}\n   242\t\n   243\t\\begin{definition}[Distance between strategies]\\label{def:strategy-distance}\n   244\t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.AreCloseStrategies}\n   245\t\t\\leanok\n   246\t\t\\uses{def:tensor-product-strategy, def:state-distance, def:povm-distance}\n   247\t\tLet $\\mathfrak G = (\\mathcal X, \\mathcal Y, \\mathcal A, \\mathcal B, \\mu, D)$ be a nonlocal game and let $\\mathcal S = (\\psi, A, B)$ and $\\mathcal S' = (\\psi', A', B')$ be strategies for $\\mathfrak G$. For $\\delta \\in [0,1]$ we say that \\emph{$\\mathcal S$ is $\\delta$-close to $\\mathcal S'$} if the following conditions hold.\n   248\t\t\\begin{enumerate}\n   249\t\t\t\\item The states $\\ket{\\psi}, \\ket{\\psi'}$ are states in the same Hilbert space $\\mathcal H_A \\ot \\mathcal H_B$ and are $\\delta$-close.\n   250\t\t\t\\item For all $x \\in \\mathcal X$ and $y \\in \\mathcal Y$, we have $A^x_a \\approx_\\delta (A')^x_a$ and $B^y_b \\approx_\\delta (B')^y_b$, with the approximations holding under the distribution $\\mu$ (i.e.\\ under its corresponding marginals), on either $\\ket{\\psi}$ or $\\ket{\\psi'}$.\n   251\t\t\\end{enumerate}\n   252\t\\end{definition}\n   253\t\n   254\t\\begin{remark}[Asymptotic reading of the distance relations]\\label{rem:asymptotic-distance}\n   255\t\tDefinitions~\\ref{def:state-distance}, \\ref{def:consistency}, and \\ref{def:povm-distance} are asymptotic: every $\\approx_\\delta$ and $\\simeq_\\delta$ statement refers to families of states and measurement families indexed by an implicit parameter $n \\in \\N$, and the $O(\\cdot)$ is taken as $n \\to \\infty$. None of these relations is a pointwise inequality with an explicit constant. By contrast, the corresponding relations used in the low individual degree chapters (Definitions~\\ref{def:simeq} and~\\ref{def:approx_delta}) carry no hidden constant. Any explicit quantitative version of the present relations therefore retains the constants absorbed into the $O(\\cdot)$; for instance, the triangle inequality of Lemma~\\ref{fact:triangle} carries a factor $2$ inside the $O(\\cdot)$.\n   256\t\\end{remark}\n   257\t\n   258\tWe record several useful facts about the consistency measure and the state-dependent distance. For the statements imported without proof, readers are referred to Sections~4.4 and~4.5 of \\cite{Natarajan2018NEEXP}.\n   259\t\n   260\t\\begin{lemma}[Consistency versus closeness; Fact 4.13 in \\cite{Natarajan2018NEEXP}]\\label{fact:agreement}\n   261\t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.opFamilyDistSq_le_two_mul_consistencyDefect, MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect_le_opFamilyDistSq_of_projective}\n   262\t\t\\leanok\n   263\t\t\\uses{def:consistency, def:povm-distance}\n   264\t\tFor POVMs $\\{A^x_a\\}$ and $\\{B^x_a\\}$, the following hold.\n   265\t\t\\begin{enumerate}\n   266\t\t\t\\item If $A^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\simeq_\\delta \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a$, then $A^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\approx_\\delta \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a$.\n   267\t\t\t\\item If $A^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\approx_\\delta \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a$ \\emph{and} $\\{A^x_a\\}$ and $\\{B^x_a\\}$ are projective measurements, then $A^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\simeq_\\delta \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a$.\n   268\t\t\\end{enumerate}\n   269\t\\end{lemma}\n   270\t\\begin{proof}\n   271\t\t\\leanok\n   272\t\t\\uses{lem:distance-consistency-term,\n   273\t\t\tlem:distance-point-distance-le-defect,\n   274\t\t\tlem:distance-projective-point-distance, lem:distance-nonnegative}\n   275\t\tStated in the source without proof; this is Fact 4.13 of \\cite{Natarajan2018NEEXP}. For the first item, expand each term $\\lVert (A^x_a \\ot \\Id - \\Id \\ot B^x_a)\\ket{\\psi} \\rVert^2$ and use $ (A^x_a)^2 \\le A^x_a$, $(B^x_a)^2 \\le B^x_a$ together with completeness of the two POVMs: summing over $a$ and averaging over $x$ bounds the total by at most twice the off-diagonal mass, which is $O(\\delta)$ by hypothesis. When both families are projective the two operator inequalities hold with equality, so the expansion equals exactly twice the off-diagonal mass; reading this identity in the other direction gives the second item.\n   276\t\\end{proof}\n   277\t\n   278\t\\begin{lemma}[Consistency from closeness with one projective family; Fact 4.14 in \\cite{Natarajan2018NEEXP}]\\label{fact:agreement-one-sided}\n   279\t\t% Status: the statement is final; no Lean declaration exists yet for the full disjunctive form, so this node carries no formalization marker.\n   280\t\t\\uses{def:consistency, def:povm-distance}\n   281\t\tLet $\\{A^x_a\\}$ and $\\{B^x_a\\}$ be POVMs. If $A^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\approx_\\delta \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a$ and either $\\{A^x_a\\}$ or $\\{B^x_a\\}$ is a projective measurement, then $A^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\simeq_{\\delta^{1/2}} \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a$.\n   282\t\\end{lemma}\n   283\t\\begin{proof}\n   284\t\t\\uses{lem:distance-projective-left-square-root}\n   285\t\tStated in the source without proof; it is Fact 4.14 of \\cite{Natarajan2018NEEXP}. Write the off-diagonal mass $\\sum_{a \\ne b} \\bra{\\psi} A^x_a \\ot B^x_b \\ket{\\psi}$ as an inner product involving $(A^x_a \\ot \\Id - \\Id \\ot B^x_a)\\ket{\\psi}$, using projectivity of one of the two families, and apply the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality; this route costs a square root in the error. Only the branch in which $\\{A^x_a\\}$ is the projective family is available, as Lemma~\\ref{lem:agreement-projective-left}; the branch in which only $\\{B^x_a\\}$ is projective is still open.\n   286\t\\end{proof}\n   287\t\n   288\t\\begin{lemma}[Left-projective branch of Lemma~\\ref{fact:agreement-one-sided}]\\label{lem:agreement-projective-left}\n   289\t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect_le_sqrt_of_projective_left}\n   290\t\t\\leanok\n   291\t\t\\uses{def:consistency, def:povm-distance}\n   292\t\tThis entry states only the branch of Lemma~\\ref{fact:agreement-one-sided} in which the left family is the projective one; it is not the full disjunctive statement of the source. Let $\\mu$ be a probability distribution on $\\mathcal X$, let $\\ket{\\psi}$ be a unit vector, and let $\\{A^x_a\\}$ be a projective measurement for every $x$. Then\n   293\t\t\\[\n   294\t\t\t\\E_x \\sum_{a \\ne b} \\bra{\\psi} A^x_a \\ot B^x_b \\ket{\\psi}\n   295\t\t\t\\leq \\sqrt{2\\, \\E_x \\sum_a \\bigl\\lVert (A^x_a \\ot \\Id - \\Id \\ot B^x_a)\\ket{\\psi} \\bigr\\rVert^2}\\,;\n   296\t\t\\]\n   297\t\tin particular, if $A^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\approx_\\delta \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a$, then $A^x_a \\ot \\Id_B \\simeq_{(2\\delta)^{1/2}} \\Id_A \\ot B^x_a$.\n   298\t\\end{lemma}\n   299\t\\begin{proof}\n   300\t\t\\leanok\n   301\t\t\\uses{lem:distance-projective-left-square-root, lem:distance-averaged-square-root}\n   302\t\tApply the pointwise estimate of Lemma~\\ref{lem:distance-projective-left-square-root} at each question $x$, then average over $x$ with Lemma~\\ref{lem:distance-averaged-square-root}.\n   303\t\\end{proof}\n   304\t\n   305\t\\begin{lemma}[Fact 4.20 in \\cite{Natarajan2018NEEXP}]\\label{fact:add-a-proj}\n   306\t\t\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.opFamilyDistSq_mul_left_le}\n   307\t\t\\leanok\n   308\t\t\\uses{def:povm-distance}\n   309\t\tLet $\\mathcal A, \\mathcal B, \\mathcal C$ be finite sets, and let $\\mu$ be a distrdding`. -/\n   425\tlemma pQApprox_ofRankReductionSigmaRangeAndSvdIdentities\n   426\t    {Outcome : Type*} [Fintype Outcome] [DecidableEq Outcome]\n   427\t    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n   428\t    (ψ : QuantumState ι)\n   429\t    (A : Measurement Outcome ι) (ζ : Error)\n   430\t    {qLayer : QLayerData Outcome ι}\n   431\t    (hRank : RankReductionWitness ψ A ζ qLayer)\n   432\t    [Nonempty (FiniteHilbertSpace.sigmaFinCarrier\n   433\t      (fun a : Outcome => (qLayer.q.outcome a).rank))]\n   434\t    (xHat : Matrix (sigmaRangeCarrier qLayer.q) ι ℂ)\n   435\t    (xHat_coisometry : xHat * xHatᴴ =\n   436\t      (1 : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op (sigmaRangeCarrier qLayer.q)))\n   437\t    (xHat_mixed :\n   438\t      (sigmaFinRangeEmbedding qLayer.q.outcome hRank.projective)ᴴ * xHat =\n   439\t        CFC.sqrt (QTotal qLayer))\n   440\t    (hψ : ψ.IsNormalized)\n   441\t    (hζ : 0 ≤ ζ) (hζ_small : ζ ≤ 1 / (4 : Error)) :\n   442\t    ∃ data : QXPLayerData Outcome ι,\n   443\t      ∃ hq : data.qLayer = sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q,\n   444\t        hq ▸ data.x =\n   445\t          (show Matrix (sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q).auxSpace.carrier ι ℂ from\n   446\t            sigmaFinRangeEmbedding qLayer.q.outcome hRank.projective) ∧\n   447\t        hq ▸ data.xHat =\n   448\t          (show Matrix (sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q).auxSpace.carrier ι ℂ from xHat) ∧\n   449\t        SDDOpRel ψ (uniformDistribution Unit)\n   450\t          (constOpFamily data.qLayer.q)\n   451\t          (constOpFamily (PFamily data))\n   452\t          (30 * zetaQuarterRoot ζ) := by\n   453\t  obtain ⟨data, hq, hdata_x, hdata_xHat⟩ :=\n   454\t    exists_qxpLayerData_ofRankReductionSigmaRangeAndSvdIdentities hRank xHat\n   455\t      xHat_coisometry xHat_mixed\n   456\t  refine ⟨data, hq, hdata_x, hdata_xHat, ?_⟩\n   457\t  exact pQApprox ψ A ζ data hψ hζ hζ_small\n   458\t    (hq.symm ▸ hRank.toSigmaRangeQLayer)\n   459\t\n   460\t/-- Apply `lem:P-Q-approx` to the positive-Gram sigma-space QXP layer.\n   461\t\n   462\tThis is the constructor-facing form of the local `Q -> X -> Xhat -> P` stage.\n   463\tThe rank-reduction witness supplies the sigma-space `X`; the positive-Gram\n   464\tpolar construction supplies `Xhat`; and the theorem concludes the paper's\n   465\t`P`-versus-`Q` approximation without any external SVD data. -/\n   466\tlemma pQApprox_ofRankReductionSigmaRangePositiveGram\n   467\t    {Outcome : Type uOutcome} [Fintype Outcome] [DecidableEq Outcome]\n   468\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n   469\t    (ψ : QuantumState ι)\n   470\t    (A : Measurement Outcome ι) (ζ : Error)\n   471\t    {qLayer : QLayerData Outcome ι}\n   472\t    (hRank : RankReductionWitness ψ A ζ qLayer)\n   473\t    [Nonempty (FiniteHilbertSpace.sigmaFinCarrier\n   474\t      (fun a : Outcome => (qLayer.q.outcome a).rank))]\n   475\t    (hψ : ψ.IsNormalized)\n   476\t    (hζ : 0 ≤ ζ) (hζ_small : ζ ≤ 1 / (4 : Error)) :\n   477\t    ∃ xHat : Matrix (sigmaRangeCarrier qLayer.q) ι ℂ,\n   478\t      xHat * xHatᴴ =\n   479\t          (1 : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op (sigmaRangeCarrier qLayer.q)) ∧\n   480\t        (sigmaFinRangeEmbedding qLayer.q.outcome hRank.projective)ᴴ * xHat =\n   481\t            CFC.sqrt (QTotal qLayer) ∧\n   482\t          ∃ data : QXPLayerData Outcome ι,\n   483\t            ∃ hq : data.qLayer = sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q,\n   484\t              hq ▸ data.x =\n   485\t                  (show Matrix (sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q).auxSpace.carrier ι ℂ from\n   486\t                    sigmaFinRangeEmbedding qLayer.q.outcome hRank.projective) ∧\n   487\t                hq ▸ data.xHat =\n   488\t                    (show Matrix (sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q).auxSpace.carrier ι ℂ from\n   489\t                      xHat) ∧\n   490\t                  SDDOpRel ψ (uniformDistribution Unit)\n   491\t                    (constOpFamily data.qLayer.q)\n   492\t                    (constOpFamily (PFamily data))\n   493\t                    (30 * zetaQuarterRoot ζ) := by\n   494\t  obtain ⟨xHat, hxHat_coisometry, hxHat_mixed, data, hq, hx, hxHat⟩ :=\n   495\t    exists_qxpLayerData_ofRankReductionSigmaRangePositiveGram hRank\n   496\t  refine ⟨xHat, hxHat_coisometry, hxHat_mixed, data, hq, hx, hxHat, ?_⟩\n   497\t  exact pQApprox ψ A ζ data hψ hζ hζ_small\n   498\t    (hq.symm ▸ hRank.toSigmaRangeQLayer)\n   499\t\n   500\t/-- Apply `lem:P-Q-approx` to the positive-Gram sigma-space QXP layer, and\n   501\talso record coisometry of the original sigma embedding `X`.\n   502\t\n   503\tThe additional hypothesis is the subnormalization of the projective `Q` family.\n   504\tUnder this hypothesis the range basis vectors chosen for distinct outcomes are\n   505\torthogonal, so the finite sigma-range embedding has orthonormal rows.  This is\n   506\tthe construction-level coisometry condition later used to preserve the fresh\n   507\toption-completion row and hence to obtain the QXP-internal comparison\n   508\t`Q_none ≤ P_none`.  An additional source-to-`Q` comparison is still required to\n   509\trecover `(optionCompletion A).outcome none ≤ P.outcome none`; see\n   510\t`docs/reports/issue-1642-restrictsome-residual-domination-obstruction.md`.\n   511\t-/\n   512\tlemma pQApprox_ofRankReductionSigmaRangePositiveGram_with_x_coisometry\n   513\t    {Outcome : Type uOutcome} [Fintype Outcome] [DecidableEq Outcome]\n   514\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n   515\t    (ψ : QuantumState ι)\n   516\t    (A : Measurement Outcome ι) (ζ : Error)\n   517\t    {qLayer : QLayerData Outcome ι}\n   518\t    (hRank : RankReductionWitness ψ A ζ qLayer)\n   519\t    (hsum_le_one :\n   520\t      (∑ a : Outcome, qLayer.q.outcome a) ≤ (1 : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op ι))\n   521\t    [Nonempty (FiniteHilbertSpace.sigmaFinCarrier\n   522\t      (fun a : Outcome => (qLayer.q.outcome a).rank))]\n   523\t    (hψ : ψ.IsNormalized)\n   524\t    (hζ : 0 ≤ ζ) (hζ_small : ζ ≤ 1 / (4 : Error)) :\n   525\t    ∃ xHat : Matrix (sigmaRangeCarrier qLayer.q) ι ℂ,\n   526\t      xHat * xHatᴴ =\n   527\t          (1 : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op (sigmaRangeCarrier qLayer.q)) ∧\n   528\t        (sigmaFinRangeEmbedding qLayer.q.outcome hRank.projective)ᴴ * xHat =\n   529\t            CFC.sqrt (QTotal qLayer) ∧\n   530\t          ∃ data : QXPLayerData Outcome ι,\n   531\t            ∃ hq : data.qLayer = sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q,\n   532\t              hq ▸ data.x =\n   533\t                  (show Matrix (sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q).auxSpace.carrier ι ℂ from\n   534\t                    sigmaFinRangeEmbedding qLayer.q.outcome hRank.projective) ∧\n   535\t                hq ▸ data.xHat =\n   536\t                    (show Matrix (sigmaRangeQLayer qLayer.q).auxSpace.carrier ι ℂ from\n   537\t                      xHat) ∧\n   538\t                  data.x * data.xᴴ =\n   539\t                    (1 : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op data.qLayer.auxSpace.carrier) ∧\n   540\t                    SDDOpRel ψ (uniformDistribution Unit)\n   541\t                      (constOpFamily data.qLayer.q)\n   542\t                      (constOpFamily (PFamily data))\n   543\t                      (30 * zetaQuarterRoot ζ) := by\n   544\t  obtain ⟨xHat, hxHat_coisometry, hxHat_mixed, data, hq, hx, hxHat, hx_coisometry⟩ :=\n   545\t    exists_qxpLayerData_ofRankReductionSigmaRangePositiveGram_with_x_coisometry\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^lemma (projectiveLowRankSum|qCompleteness|sqrtQCompleteness)|''^theorem (projectiveLowRankSum|qCompleteness|sqrtQCompleteness)'\"' MIPStarRE/LDT/MakingMeasurementsProjective -g '*.lean' | cut -d: -f1-2 | uniq\"","agralTruncationStatement_of_witness {Outcome : Type uOutcome}\n    40\t    [Fintype Outcome] [DecidableEq Outcome]\n    41\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n    42\t    (ψ : QuantumState ι) (A : Measurement Outcome ι) (ζ : Error)\n    43\t    (R : OpFamily Outcome ι)\n    44\t    (hwitness : RoundingToProjectorsWitness ψ A ζ R) :\n    45\t    SpectralTruncationStatement ψ A ζ :=\n    46\t  ⟨R, hwitness.projective, hwitness.closeness, hwitness.sum_eq_total,\n    47\t    hwitness.total_le⟩\n    48\t\n    49\tnamespace SpectralTruncationStatement\n    50\t\n    51\t/-- Paper origin: `references/ldt-paper/orthonormalization.tex:414-531`\n    52\t(`\\label{lem:projective-non-measurement}`; rounding-to-projectors lemma\n    53\twith `2√ζ` closeness and `(1+2√ζ)·I` total bound).\n    54\t\n    55\tConvert a spectral-truncation statement back to the rounded-projector\n    56\twitness consumed by the QXP rank-reduction layer.\n    57\t\n    58\t**Source:** This is a source-faithful structural conversion of the rounded-family\n    59\tconclusion of the cited lemma. It does not recover the source almost-projective\n    60\testimate, because that estimate is not a field of `SpectralTruncationStatement`;\n    61\trank-reduction constructors which need it therefore keep it as a separate\n    62\thypothesis. -/\n    63\ttheorem toRoundingToProjectorsWitness {Outcome : Type uOutcome}\n    64\t    [Fintype Outcome] [DecidableEq Outcome]\n    65\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n    66\t    {ψ : QuantumState ι} {A : Measurement Outcome ι} {ζ : Error}\n    67\t    (h : SpectralTruncationStatement ψ A ζ) :\n    68\t    RoundingToProjectorsWitness ψ A ζ h.roundedFamily where\n    69\t  projective := h.projective\n    70\t  closeness := h.closeness\n    71\t  sum_eq_total := h.sum_eq_total\n    72\t  total_le := h.total_le\n    73\t\n    74\tend SpectralTruncationStatement\n    75\t\n    76\t/-! ### Rank-reduction from spectral truncation -/\n    77\t\n    78\t/-- Feed a spectral-truncation statement into the QXP rank-reduction layer.\n    79\t\n    80\tThe statement `SpectralTruncationStatement` remembers the rounded projectors\n    81\tand their distance from the source measurement.  The rank-reduction witness also\n    82\trecords the source almost-projectivity estimate, so that estimate remains an\n    83\texplicit hypothesis here.  This is the precise interface needed when the\n    84\torthonormalization spectral input is followed by the paper's\n    85\t`Q -> X -> Xhat -> P` repair layer. -/\n    86\tlemma projectiveLowRankSum_of_spectralTruncationStatement\n    87\t    {Outcome : Type uOutcome} [Fintype Outcome] [DecidableEq Outcome]\n    88\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]\n    89\t    (ψ : QuantumState ι) (A : Measurement Outcome ι) (ζ : Error)\n    90\t    (hψ : ψ.IsNormalized)\n    91\t    (hζ : 0 ≤ ζ) (hζ_le : ζ ≤ 1 / 4)\n    92\t    (hSpectral : SpectralTruncationStatement ψ A ζ)\n    93\t    (hsource :\n    94\t      ∑ a, ev ψ (A.outcome a - A.outcome a * A.outcome a) ≤ 2 * ζ) :\n    95\t    ∃ data : QLayerData Outcome ι,\n    96\t      RankReductionWitness ψ A ζ data :=\n    97\t  projectiveLowRankSum_of_roundingWitness ψ A ζ hψ hζ hζ_le hSpectral.roundedFamily\n    98\t    hSpectral.toRoundingToProjectorsWitness hsource\n    99\t\n   100\t/-- **Rank reduction** (`\\label{lem:projective-low-rank-sum}`).\n   101\t\n   102\tPaper origin: `references/ldt-paper/orthonormalization.tex:540-658`.\n   103\t\n   104\tThe paper first applies `\\label{lem:projective-non-measurement}` to obtain the\n   105\trounded projective family `R_a`, and then performs the rank-reduction argument.\n   106\tThis theorem keeps that source-facing boundary: the rounded family is produced\n   107\tinternally from the source almost-projectivity estimate and is then passed to\n   108\tthe internal constructor `projectiveLowRankSum_of_roundingWitness`. -/\n   109\tlemma projectiveLowRankSum {Outcome : Type uOutcome}\n   110\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]\n   111\t    [Fintype Outcome]\n   112\t    (ψ : QuantumState ι)\n   113\t    (A : Measurement Outcome ι) (ζ : Error)\n   114\t    (hψ : ψ.IsNormalized)\n   115\t    (hζ : 0 ≤ ζ) (hζ_le : ζ ≤ 1 / 4)\n   116\t    (source_almost_projective :\n   117\t      ∑ a, ev ψ (A.outcome a - A.outcome a * A.outcome a) ≤ 2 * ζ) :\n   118\t    ∃ data : QLayerData Outcome ι,\n   119\t      RankReductionWitness ψ A ζ data := by\n   120\t  classical\n   121\t  obtain ⟨q, hrounded⟩ :=\n   122\t    projectiveNonMeasurement_of_sourceAlmostProjective_two_mul_full\n   123\t      ψ A ζ hψ source_almost_projective\n   124\t  exact projectiveLowRankSum_of_roundingWitness ψ A ζ hψ hζ hζ_le q hrounded\n   125\t    source_almost_projective\n   126\t\n   127\tend MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective\n     1\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.QXPLayer.RankReduction.LowRank\n     2\t\n     3\t/-!\n     4\t# Section 5 — Q/X/XHat/P q-completeness\n     5\t\n     6\tCompleteness estimates for the rank-reduced `Q` family in the paper's\n     7\t`Q/X/XHat/P` intermediate layer.\n     8\t-/\n     9\t\n    10\topen scoped BigOperators MatrixOrder Matrix ComplexOrder\n    11\t\n    12\tnamespace MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective\n    13\t\n    14\topen MIPStarRE.LDT\n    15\t\n    16\tnoncomputable section\n    17\t\n    18\t/-- Under the small-error hypothesis `ζ ≤ 1/4`, the truncation error is at most `1/2`. -/\n    19\tlemma spectralTruncationError_le_half (ζ : Error)\n    20\t    (_hζ : 0 ≤ ζ) (hζq : ζ ≤ 1 / (4 : Error)) :\n    21\t    spectralTruncationError ζ ≤ 1 / (2 : Error) := by\n    22\t  -- Scalar bookkeeping for `ζ ≤ 1/4`: `√ζ ≤ 1/2`.\n    23\t  have hquarter : Real.sqrt (1 / (4 : Error)) = 1 / (2 : Error) := by norm_num\n    24\t  have hsqrt : Real.sqrt ζ ≤ 1 / (2 : Error) := by\n    25\t    exact hquarter ▸ Real.sqrt_le_sqrt hζq\n    26\t  simpa [spectralTruncationError, Real.sqrt_eq_rpow] using hsqrt\n    27\t\n    28\t/-- Under the small-error hypothesis `ζ ≤ 1/4`, the spectral truncation error\n    29\tis bounded by the fourth-root error scale used in the `Q/X/XHat/P` layer. -/\n    30\tlemma spectralTruncationError_le_zetaQuarterRoot (ζ : Error)\n    31\t    (hζ : 0 ≤ ζ) (hζq : ζ ≤ 1 / (4 : Error)) :\n    32\t    spectralTruncationError ζ ≤ zetaQuarterRoot ζ := by\n    33\t  have hζ1 : ζ ≤ 1 := by linarith\n    34\t  dsimp [spectralTruncationError, zetaQuarterRoot]\n    35\t  exact Real.rpow_le_rpow_of_exponent_ge' hζ hζ1 (by positivity)\n    36\t    (by norm_num : (1 : Error) / 2 ≥ 1 / 4)\n    37\t\n    38\t/-- **Completeness of `Q`** (`lem:Q-completeness`).\n    39\t\n    40\tIf `Q_a` is the rank-reduced family from `lem:projective-low-rank-sum`, then\n    41\tits total operator `Q` has expectation at least `1 - 11 ζ^(1/4)`. -/\n    42\tlemma qCompleteness {Outcome : Type*}\n    43\t    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n    44\t    [Fintype Outcome]\n    45\t    (ψ : QuantumState ι)\n    46\t    (A : Measurement Outcome ι) (ζ : Error)\n    47\t    (data : QLayerData Outcome ι)\n    48\t    (hψ : ψ.IsNormalized)\n    49\t    (hζ : 0 ≤ ζ)\n    50\t    (hζ_small : ζ ≤ 1 / (4 : Error)) :\n    51\t    RankReductionWitness ψ A ζ data →\n    52\t      ev ψ (QTotal data) ≥ 1 - 11 * zetaQuarterRoot ζ := by\n    53\t  intro hRank\n    54\t  let diagA : Error := ∑ a : Outcome, ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a)\n    55\t  let qMass : Error := ev ψ (QTotal data)\n    56\t  let overlap : Error := ∑ a : Outcome, ev ψ (A.outcome a * Qa data a)\n    57\t  have hsdd :\n    58\t      qSDDOp ψ (A.toSubMeas : OpFamily Outcome ι) data.q ≤\n    59\t        roundingToProjectiveError ζ := by\n    60\t    simpa [SDDOpRel, sddErrorOp, avgOver, uniformDistribution, constOpFamily, qSDDOp]\n    61\t      using hRank.closeness.squaredDistanceBound\n    62\t  have hdiagA_nonneg : 0 ≤ diagA := by\n    63\t    unfold diagA\n    64\t    exact Finset.sum_nonneg fun a _ => by\n    65\t      simpa [Measurement.outcome_hermitian] using ev_adjoint_self_nonneg ψ (A.outcome a)\n    66\t  have hdiagA_le_one : diagA ≤ 1 := by\n    67\t    simpa [diagA] using\n    68\t      MIPStarRE.LDT.Preliminaries.subMeas_diagMass_le_one ψ hψ A.toSubMeas\n    69\t  have hsqrt_diagA_le_one : Real.sqrt diagA ≤ 1 := by\n    70\t    simpa using Real.sqrt_le_sqrt hdiagA_le_one\n    71\t  have hdiagA_lb : 1 - 2 * ζ ≤ diagA := by\n    72\t    have hsource := hRank.source_almost_projective\n    73\t    have hsum :\n    74\t        ∑ a, ev ψ (A.outcome a - A.outcome a * A.outcome a) = 1 - diagA := by\n    75\t      calc\n    76\t        ∑ a, ev ψ (A.outcome a - A.outcome a * A.outcome a)\n    77\t            = ∑ a, (ev ψ (A.outcome a) - ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a)) := by\n    78\t                refine Finset.sum_congr rfl ?_\n    79\t                intro a _\n    80\t                exact ev_sub ψ (A.outcome a) (A.outcome a * A.outcome a)\n    81\t        _ = (∑ a, ev ψ (A.outcome a)) - ∑ a, ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a) := by\n    82\t              rw [Finset.sum_sub_distrib]\n    83\t        _ = 1 - diagA := by\n    84\t              rw [← ev_sum ψ A.outcome, A.sum_eq]\n    85\t              simp [diagA, ev_one_of_isNormalized ψ hψ]\n    86\t    linarith [hsource, hsum]\n    87\t  have hqtotal_nonneg : 0 ≤ QTotal data := by\n    88\t    rw [← hRank.sum_eq_total]\n    89\t    exact Finset.sum_nonneg fun a _ => hRank.outcome_nonneg a\n    90\t  have hq_nonneg : 0 ≤ qMass := by\n    91\t    exact ev_nonneg_of_psd ψ (QTotal data) hqtotal_nonneg\n    92\t  have hdiagQ_eq :\n    93\t      ∑ a : Outcome, ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a) = qMass := by\n    94\t    calc\n    95\t      ∑ a : Outcome, ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a)\n    96\t          = ∑ a : Outcome, ev ψ (Qa data a) := by\n    97\t              refine Finset.sum_congr rfl ?_\n    98\t              intro a _\n    99\t              rw [(hRank.projective a).isIdempotentElem.eq]\n   100\t      _ = ev ψ (QTotal data) := by\n   101\t            rw [← ev_sum ψ (Qa data), hRank.sum_eq_total]\n   102\t  have hoverlap_le : overlap ≤ Real.sqrt diagA * Real.sqrt qMass := by\n   103\t    have hoverlap_abs :\n   104\t        |overlap| ≤ Real.sqrt diagA * Real.sqrt qMass := by\n   105\t      calc\n   106\t        |overlap|\n   107\t            = |∑ a : Outcome, ev ψ (A.outcome a * Qa data a)| := by\n   108\t                simp [overlap]\n   109\t        _ ≤ ∑ a : Outcome, |ev ψ (A.outcome a * Qa data a)| := by\n   110\t              exact Finset.abs_sum_le_sum_abs _ _\n   111\t        _ ≤ ∑ a : Outcome,\n   112\t              Real.sqrt (ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a)) *\n   113\t                Real.sqrt (ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a)) := by\n   114\t              refine Finset.sum_le_sum ?_\n   115\t              intro a _\n   116\t              simpa [Measurement.outcome_hermitian,\n   117\t                (hRank.projective a).isSelfAdjoint.isHermitian.eq] using\n   118\t                ev_abs_mul_le_sqrt ψ (A.outcome a) (Qa data a)\n   119\t        _ ≤ Real.sqrt diagA *\n   120\t              Real.sqrt (∑ a : Outcome, ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a)) := by\n   121\t              simpa [diagA] using\n   122\t                Real.sum_sqrt_mul_sqrt_le (s := Finset.univ)\n   123\t                  (f := fun a => ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a))\n   124\t                  (g := fun a => ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a))\n   125\t                  (fun a => by\n   126\t                    simpa [Measurement.outcome_hermitian] using\n   127\t                      ev_adjoint_self_nonneg ψ (A.outcome a))\n   128\t                  (fun a => by\n   129\t                    simpa [(hRank.projective a).isSelfAdjoint.isHermitian.eq] using\n   130\t                      ev_adjoint_self_nonneg ψ (Qa data a))\n   131\t        _ = Real.sqrt diagA * Real.sqrt qMass := by rw [hdiagQ_eq]\n   132\t    exact (abs_le.mp hoverlap_abs).2\n   133\t  have h_expand :\n   134\t      qSDDOp ψ (A.toSubMeas : OpFamily Outcome ι) data.q =\n   135\t        diagA + qMass - 2 * overlap := by\n   136\t    unfold qSDDOp qSDDCore\n   137\t    calc\n   138\t      ∑ a, ev ψ ((A.outcome a - Qa data a)ᴴ * (A.outcome a - Qa data a))\n   139\t        = ∑ a, (ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a) +\n   140\t            ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a) -\n   141\t            2 * ev ψ (A.outcome a * Qa data a)) := by\n   142\t              refine Finset.sum_congr rfl ?_\n   143\t              intro a _\n   144\t              have hcomm :\n   145\t                  ev ψ (Qa data a * A.outcome a) =\n   146\t                    ev ψ (A.outcome a * Qa data a) := by\n   147\t                exact ev_mul_comm_of_psd ψ _ _ (hRank.outcome_nonneg a) (A.outcome_pos a)\n   148\t              calc\n   149\t                ev ψ ((A.outcome a - Qa data a)ᴴ * (A.outcome a - Qa data a))\n   150\t                    = ev ψ ((A.outcome a * A.outcome a -\n   151\t                        A.outcome a * Qa data a) -\n   152\t                        (Qa data a * A.outcome a -\n   153\t                          Qa data a * Qa data a)) := by\n   154\t                          congr 1\n   155\t                          simp [sub_mul, mul_sub, Measurement.outcome_hermitian,\n   156\t                            (hRank.projective a).isSelfAdjoint.isHermitian.eq]\n   157\t                          abel\n   158\t                _ = ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a) -\n   159\t                      ev ψ (A.outcome a * Qa data a) -\n   160\t                      (ev ψ (Qa data a * A.outcome a) -\n   161\t                        ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a)) := by\n   162\t                        rw [ev_sub, ev_sub, ev_sub]\n   163\t                _ = ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a) +\n   164\t                      ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a) -\n   165\t                      2 * ev ψ (A.outcome a * Qa data a) := by\n   166\t                        rw [hcomm]\n   167\t                        ring\n   168\t      _ = (∑ a, ev ψ (A.outcome a * A.outcome a)) +\n   169\t            (∑ a, ev ψ (Qa data a * Qa data a)) -\n   170\t            2 * ∑ a, ev ψ (A.outcome a * Qa data a) := by\n   171\t              rw [Finset.sum_sub_distrib, Finset.sum_add_distrib, Finset.mul_sum]\n   172\t      _ = diagA + qMass - 2 * overlap := by\n   173\t            simp [diagA, overlap, hdiagQ_eq]\n   174\t  have hsq_gap :\n   175\t      (Real.sqrt qMass - Real.sqrt diagA) ^ (2 : Nat) ≤\n   176\t        roundingToProjectiveError ζ := by\n   177\t    calc\n   178\t      (Real.sqrt qMass - Real.sqrt diagA) ^ (2 : Nat)\n   179\t          = qMass + diagA - 2 * (Real.sqrt diagA * Real.sqrt qMass) := by\n   180\t              nlinarith [Real.sq_sqrt hq_nonneg, Real.sq_sqrt hdiagA_nonneg]\n   181\t      _ ≤ qMass + diagA - 2 * overlap := by\n   182\t            nlinarith [hoverlap_le]\n   183\t      _ = qSDDOp ψ (A.toSubMeas : OpFamily Outcome ι) data.q := by\n   184\t            rw [h_expand]\n   185\t            ring\n   186\t      _ ≤ roundingToProjectiveError ζ := hsdd\n   187\t  have hround_nonneg : 0 ≤ roundingToProjectiveError ζ := by\n   188\t    dsimp [roundingToProjectiveError]\n   189\t    exact mul_nonneg (by norm_num) (spectralTruncationError_nonneg hζ)\n   190\t  have habs :\n   191\t      |Real.sqrt qMass - Real.sqrt diagA| ≤ Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) := by\n   192\t    refine abs_le_of_sq_le_sq' ?_ (Real.sqrt_nonneg _) |>.2\n   193\t    calc\n   194\t      |Real.sqrt qMass - Real.sqrt diagA| ^ 2\n   195\t          = (Real.sqrt qMass - Real.sqrt diagA) ^ (2 : Nat) := by\n   196\t              rw [sq_abs]\n   197\t      _ ≤ roundingToProjectiveError ζ := hsq_gap\n   198\t      _ = (Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ)) ^ (2 : Nat) := by\n   199\t            calc\n   200\t              roundingToProjectiveError ζ\n   201\t                  = Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) *\n   202\t                      Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) := by\n   203\t                        nlinarith [Real.sq_sqrt hround_nonneg]\n   204\t              _ = (Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ)) ^ (2 : Nat) := by\n   205\t                    simp [pow_two]\n   206\t  have hsqrt_q_lb :\n   207\t      Real.sqrt qMass ≥ Real.sqrt diagA - Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) := by\n   208\t    have hleft := (abs_le.mp habs).1\n   209\t    linarith\n   210\t  have hq_lb :\n   211\t      qMass ≥ diagA - 2 * Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) := by\n   212\t    let s : Error := Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ)\n   213\t    let x : Error := Real.sqrt qMass\n   214\t    let y : Error := Real.sqrt diagA\n   215\t    have hxy : x ≥ y - s := by\n   216\t      dsimp [x, y, s]\n   217\t      exact hsqrt_q_lb\n   218\t    by_cases hys : y ≤ s\n   219\t    · have htarget : diagA - 2 * Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) ≤ 0 := by\n   220\t        dsimp [y, s] at hys ⊢\n   221\t        nlinarith [Real.sq_sqrt hdiagA_nonneg,\n   222\t          Real.sqrt_nonneg diagA,\n   223\t          Real.sqrt_nonneg (roundingToProjectiveError ζ),\n   224\t          mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.mpr hsqrt_diagA_le_one)\n   225\t            (Real.sqrt_nonneg diagA)]\n   226\t      linarith\n   227\t    · have hs_le_y : s ≤ y := le_of_not_ge hys\n   228\t      have hy_sub_nonneg : 0 ≤ y - s := by linarith\n   229\t      have hx_sq_ge : x ^ (2 : Nat) ≥ (y - s) ^ (2 : Nat) := by\n   230\t        nlinarith\n   231\t      have hx_sq_ge' :\n   232\t          qMass ≥ diagA -\n   233\t            2 * Real.sqrt diagA * Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) +\n   234\t            roundingToProjectiveError ζ := by\n   235\t        dsimp [x, y, s] at hx_sq_ge\n   236\t        nlinarith [hx_sq_ge, Real.sq_sqrt hq_nonneg, Real.sq_sqrt hdiagA_nonneg,\n   237\t          Real.sq_sqrt hround_nonneg]\n   238\t      have hcross :\n   239\t          2 * Real.sqrt diagA * Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) ≤\n   240\t            2 * Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) := by\n   241\t        have hmul :\n   242\t            Real.sqrt diagA * Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) ≤\n   243\t              1 * Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) := by\n   244\t          exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hsqrt_diagA_le_one (Real.sqrt_nonneg _)\n   245\t        nlinarith\n   246\t      linarith [hx_sq_ge', hcross, hround_nonneg]\n   247\t  have hzeta_term :\n   248\t      2 * ζ ≤ 2 * zetaQuarterRoot ζ := by\n   249\t    gcongr\n   250\t    have hζ1 : ζ ≤ 1 := by linarith\n   251\t    dsimp [zetaQuarterRoot]\n   252\t    simpa [Real.rpow_one] using\n   253\t      (Real.rpow_le_rpow_of_exponent_ge' hζ hζ1 (by positivity)\n   254\t        (by norm_num : (1 : Error) ≥ 1 / 4))\n   255\t  have hround_term :\n   256\t      2 * Real.sqrt (roundingToProjectiveError ζ) ≤ 8 * zetaQuarterRoot ζ := by\n   257\t    have hsqrt_rpow :\n   258\t        Real.sqrt (ζ ^ (1 / (2 : Error))) = zetaQuarterRoot ζ := by\n   259\t      rw [Real.sqrt_eq_rpow, zetaQuarterRoot, ← Real.rpow_mul hζ]\n   260\t      congr 1\n     1\timport MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.QXPLayer.RankReduction.Sigma\n     2\t\n     3\t/-!\n     4\t# Section 5 — Q/X/XHat/P low-rank truncation\n     5\t\n     6\tRank-reduction auxiliary-space constructions and the low-rank truncation branch for\n     7\tthe paper's `Q/X/XHat/P` intermediate layer.\n     8\t-/\n     9\t\n    10\topen scoped BigOperators MatrixOrder Matrix ComplexOrder\n    11\t\n    12\tnamespace MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective\n    13\t\n    14\topen MIPStarRE.LDT\n    15\t\n    16\tnoncomputable section\n    17\t\n    18\tuniverse uOutcome uι\n    19\t\n    20\t/-- Concrete auxiliary-space construction from a direct total-rank bound. -/\n    21\tlemma projectiveLowRankSum_auxData_of_rank_bound {Outcome : Type uOutcome}\n    22\t    [Fintype Outcome] [Nonempty Outcome]\n    23\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [Nonempty ι]\n    24\t    (m : Outcome → ℕ)\n    25\t    (hm : ∑ a, m a ≤ Fintype.card ι) :\n    26\t    ∃ auxSpace : FiniteHilbertSpace.{uι}, ∃ t : ProjMeas Outcome auxSpace.carrier,\n    27\t      t.total = 1 ∧ Fintype.card auxSpace.carrier ≤ Fintype.card ι := by\n    28\t  classical\n    29\t  by_cases hsigma : Nonempty (FiniteHilbertSpace.sigmaFinCarrier m)\n    30\t  · letI := hsigma\n    31\t    let auxSpace : FiniteHilbertSpace.{uι} := FiniteHilbertSpace.sigmaFin m\n    32\t    refine ⟨auxSpace, sigmaFinProjMeas m, ?_⟩\n    33\t    refine ⟨rfl, ?_⟩\n    34\t    have hcard :\n    35\t        Fintype.card (FiniteHilbertSpace.sigmaFinCarrier m) ≤ Fintype.card ι :=\n    36\t      sigmaFinCard_le_of_sum_le (ι := ι) m hm\n    37\t    change Fintype.card (ULift (FiniteHilbertSpace.sigmaFinCarrier m)) ≤ Fintype.card ι\n    38\t    rw [Fintype.card_ulift]\n    39\t    exact hcard\n    40\t  · let a0 : Outcome := Classical.choice (inferInstance : Nonempty Outcome)\n    41\t    let auxSpace : FiniteHilbertSpace.{uι} :=\n    42\t      { carrier := ULift.{uι} Unit\n    43\t        instFintype := inferInstance\n    44\t        instDecidableEq := inferInstance\n    45\t        instNonempty := inferInstance }\n    46\t    refine ⟨auxSpace, pointProjMeas a0, ?_⟩\n    47\t    refine ⟨rfl, ?_⟩\n    48\t    have hcard_pos : 0 < Fintype.card ι := Fintype.card_pos_iff.mpr inferInstance\n    49\t    simpa [auxSpace] using Nat.succ_le_of_lt hcard_pos\n    50\t\n    51\t/-- Concrete auxiliary-space construction for the exact-projector case.\n    52\t\n    53\tWhen the honest sigma-carrier `Σ a, Fin (rank R_a)` is nonempty, we use its\n    54\tlifted finite-enumeration model. If all ranks vanish, then that carrier is\n    55\tempty, but `FiniteHilbertSpace` requires a nonempty carrier; in that degenerate\n    56\tbranch we fall back to the one-point space `ULift Unit`. -/\n    57\tlemma projectiveLowRankSum_auxData_of_projectors {Outcome : Type uOutcome}\n    58\t    [Fintype Outcome] [Nonempty Outcome]\n    59\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]\n    60\t    (R : Outcome → MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op ι)\n    61\t    (hproj : ∀ a, MIPStarRE.Quantum.IsProj (R a))\n    62\t    (htotal_le_one : (∑ a, R a) ≤ (1 : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op ι)) :\n    63\t    ∃ auxSpace : FiniteHilbertSpace.{uι}, ∃ t : ProjMeas Outcome auxSpace.carrier,\n    64\t      t.total = 1 ∧ Fintype.card auxSpace.carrier ≤ Fintype.card ι := by\n    65\t  classical\n    66\t  let m : Outcome → ℕ := fun a => (R a).rank\n    67\t  exact projectiveLowRankSum_auxData_of_rank_bound (m := m)\n    68\t    (by simpa [m] using sum_rank_le_card_of_projectors_le_one R hproj htotal_le_one)\n    69\t\n    70\t/-- Concrete rank-reduction construction once the rounded family is already an exact\n    71\tprojector submeasurement `∑_a R_a ≤ I`.\n    72\t\n    73\tThis exact-projector branch is currently kept for the blueprint cross-reference\n    74\tto the paper's `r ≤ d` statement; the public theorem routes through\n    75\t`projectiveLowRankSum_of_rank_bound` after #726. -/\n    76\tlemma projectiveLowRankSum_of_projectors {Outcome : Type uOutcome}\n    77\t    {ι : Type uι} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]\n    78\t    [Fintype Outcome] [Nonempty Outcome]\n    79\t    (ψ : QuantumState ι)\n   antumState.IsNormalized\n   156\t  have hnorm :\n   157\t      MIPStarRE.Quantum.normalizedTrace (leftMarginalDensity ψ.density) =\n   158\t        MIPStarRE.Quantum.normalizedTrace ψ.density := by\n   159\t    simpa [leftTensor_one] using\n   160\t      normalizedTrace_leftMarginalDensity_mul_eq (ρ := ψ.density)\n   161\t        (X := (1 : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op ιA))\n   162\t  simpa [leftMarginalState] using hnorm.trans hψ\n   163\t\n   164\t/-- Local evaluation in the left marginal equals bipartite evaluation of\n   165\tthe left tensor placement. -/\n   166\tlemma leftMarginal_ev_eq {ιA ιB : Type*}\n   167\t    [Fintype ιA] [DecidableEq ιA] [Fintype ιB] [DecidableEq ιB] [Nonempty ιB]\n   168\t    (ψ : QuantumState (ιA × ιB)) (X : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op ιA) :\n   169\t    ev ψ (leftTensor (ι₂ := ιB) X) = ev (leftMarginalState ψ) X := by\n   170\t  unfold ev\n   171\t  rw [← Complex.ofReal_inj]\n   172\t  simp [normalizedTrace_leftMarginalDensity_mul_eq (ρ := ψ.density) (X := X),\n   173\t    leftMarginalState]\n   174\t\n   175\tprivate def rightDiagBlock {ιA ιB : Type*}\n   176\t    [Fintype ιA] [DecidableEq ιA] [Fintype ιB] [DecidableEq ιB]\n   177\t    (M : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op (ιA × ιB)) (a : ιA) :\n   178\t    MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op ιB :=\n   179\t  M.submatrix (fun i => (a, i)) (fun j => (a, j))\n   180\t\n   181\tprivate def rightMarginalDensity {ιA ιB : Type*}\n   182\t    [Fintype ιA] [DecidableEq ιA] [Fintype ιB] [DecidableEq ιB] [Nonempty ιA]\n   183\t    (ρ : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op (ιA × ιB)) : MIPStarRE.Quantum.Op ιB :=\n   184\t  ((((Fintype.card ιA : Error) : Error)⁻¹ : Error) : ℂ) •\n   185\t    ∑ a : ιA, rightDiagBlock ρ a\n   310\t    simpa [Real.rpow_one] using\n   311\t      (Real.rpow_le_rpow_of_exponent_ge'\n   312\t        (show 0 ≤ (1 / (4 : Error)) by positivity)\n   313\t        (show (1 / (4 : Error)) ≤ 1 by norm_num)\n   314\t        (show 0 ≤ (1 / (4 : Error)) by positivity)\n   315\t        (by norm_num : (1 / (4 : Error)) ≤ 1))\n   316\t  have hquarter_le : (1 / (4 : Error)) ≤ Real.rpow ζ (1 / (4 : Error)) :=\n   317\t    le_trans hquarter_le_rpow hq_rpow_le\n   318\t  have hscaled : (84 : Error) * (1 / (4 : Error)) ≤ orthonormalizationMainLemmaError ζ := by\n   319\t    dsimp [orthonormalizationMainLemmaError]\n   320\t    exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hquarter_le (by norm_num)\n   321\t  have hone : (1 : Error) ≤ (84 : Error) * (1 / (4 : Error)) := by norm_num\n   322\t  exact hone.trans hscale