e strategy under\n  1016\t\tanalysis (Lemma~\\ref{lem:projective-strategy-setup} and the convention\n  1017\t\tfollowing it), assumed symmetric in the sense of\n  1018\t\tDefinition~\\ref{def:symmetric-game}: the state $\\ket{\\psi}$ is\n  1019\t\tinvariant under exchanging registers $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$, and\n  1020\t\tboth players measure the same operators. Let $\\ket{\\hat{\\psi}}$ be the\n  1021\t\texpanded state~\\eqref{eq:def-psihat}, let\n  1022\t\t\\[\n  1023\t\t\t\\sigma \\colon\\;\n  1024\t\t\t\\mathsf{A} \\leftrightarrow \\mathsf{B},\\quad\n  1025\t\t\t\\mathsf{A}' \\leftrightarrow \\mathsf{B}',\\quad\n  1026\t\t\t\\mathsf{A}'' \\leftrightarrow \\mathsf{B}''\\,,\n  1027\t\t\t\\qquad\\qquad\n  1028\t\t\t\\theta \\colon\\;\n  1029\t\t\t\\mathsf{A} \\leftrightarrow \\mathsf{B},\\quad\n  1030\t\t\t\\mathsf{A}' \\leftrightarrow \\mathsf{A}''\\,,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
